  <running_head>EVANGELII, SECULI, IV.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>capitis</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">sententiæ. Deinde verum est, allo-</l>
    <l n="2">quitur Apostolus Hebræos, nempe iux-</l>
    <l n="3">ta communem consuetudinem Apo-</l>
    <l n="4">stolis usitatam, qui sine distinctione</l>
    <l n="5">verba ad omnes dirigunt, ac si eiusdem</l>
    <l n="6">essent conditionis, cùm tamen magna</l>
    <l n="7">sit distinctio. In priori ad Corinthios</l>
    <l n="8">&amp; epistola ad Galatas omnes repre-</l>
    <l n="9">hendit communiter, cùm procul du-</l>
    <l n="10">bio multi inter ipsos reprehensione</l>
    <l n="11">ista indigni fuerint. Idem dicendum</l>
    <l n="12">de epistola ad Hebræos.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Locum ipsum Apostoli quod concer-</l>
    <l n="14">nit, explicatio eius ex antecedentibus</l>
    <l n="15">est desumenda. Capite quinto v. 12.</l>
    <l n="16">incepit Apostolus disputare de Hebræ-</l>
    <l n="17">orum in fide Evangelica institutione,</l>
    <l n="18">dicens, <i>ipsos equidem de Christo Pontifice</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>nostro satis instilutos fuisse, ita ut pro tem-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>poris ratione oportuerit ipsos esse Doctores:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>sed tamen propter segnitiem factos esse</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>ἀπείρως λόγω δικαιοσύνης.</i> Exprobrationi</l>
    <l n="23">huic subiicit adhortationem verf. 1.</l>
    <l n="24">capitis</l>
  </main_text>
